---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GradientText from "../components/GradientText.astro";
import PlayableNav from "../components/PlayableNav.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Playable Ads | Development, QA, and Release Readiness | Aniloom Technologies" description="Playable ad development and release-quality support, connected through the Aniloom Playable Quality System." image="/assets/images/editorial/playable-ads-v2.webp" imageAlt="Editorial illustration of playable-ad interaction states and release readiness." imageWidth={1400} imageHeight={1050}>
  <main id="main-content">
    <PlayableNav />
    <section class="page-hero page-hero--service section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Games & Playable Experiences</p>
      <h1 data-reveal>Build the playable. Make the release decision with <GradientText>evidence.</GradientText></h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lead" data-reveal>Aniloom develops focused HTML5/WebGL experiences and helps teams review existing playables against the journey, responsive states, variants, and platform constraints that matter.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__actions" data-reveal><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss a playable</button><a class="text-link" href="#choose-path">Choose a path <span>↓</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <figure class="service-artwork section-shell" data-reveal>
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/assets/images/editorial/playable-ads-v2.avif" type="image/avif" />
        <img src="/assets/images/editorial/playable-ads-v2.webp" alt="An editorial sequence of interactive states connected by a cyan path, with a yellow decision point marking the intended action before review and release." width="1400" height="1050" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </picture>
    </figure>

    <section class="entry-points section-shell section-pad" id="choose-path">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Choose the useful starting point</p><h2>New build or release-quality review?</h2></div><p>Both paths use the same product view. The difference is whether Aniloom is implementing the experience or reviewing an existing playable for the next release decision.</p></div>
      <div class="path-grid">
        <a class="path-card" href="/playable-ads/development/" data-reveal><span>01 / Development</span><h2>We need a playable built.</h2><p>Shape the concept, interaction flow, implementation, responsive behavior, variants, and release preparation as one connected delivery.</p><strong>Explore development <i>↗</i></strong></a>
        <a class="path-card" href="/playable-ads/qa-release-readiness/" data-reveal><span>02 / QA & Release</span><h2>We have a playable to review.</h2><p>Map the risks, examine meaningful states and orientations, test the end-user journey, record corrections, and make the release disposition visible.</p><strong>Explore QA & release readiness <i>↗</i></strong></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="system-band section-pad">
      <div class="section-shell">
        <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Aniloom Playable Quality System</p><h2>Development and QA share the same product view.</h2></div><p>The system connects implementation with layout, scale, typography, responsive states, visual hierarchy, and the end-user journey.</p></div>
        <div class="system-flow" data-reveal><span>Intent</span><i></i><span>Meaningful states</span><i></i><span>Review</span><i></i><span>Correction</span><i></i><span>Disposition</span></div>
        <div class="system-actions" data-reveal><a class="text-link" href="/playable-ads/how-we-work/">See the complete workflow <span>↗</span></a><p class="system-note">This is Aniloom’s working method, not a certification, provider guarantee, or claim of campaign performance.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="deliverable section-shell section-pad">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Connected concerns</p><h2>What the system keeps in view.</h2></div><p>The exact scope changes by engagement. These concerns stay connected instead of moving through isolated creative, engineering, and QA handoffs.</p></div>
      <div class="deliverable-grid">
        <div data-reveal><span>Intent and journey</span><p>The action the experience should support, the meaningful steps, and the route to its campaign action.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Responsive experience</span><p>Layout, scale, fonts, hierarchy, controls, and important states across portrait and landscape.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Variants and platforms</span><p>Agreed format constraints, integrations, links, end cards, localization, and environment-specific behavior.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Evidence and ownership</span><p>Saved corrections, retest results, open risks, responsibilities, and a clear release disposition.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="callout section-shell section-pad" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Start with the current state</p><h2>Bring the brief or the build.</h2><p>Tell us what exists, what needs to happen next, and which constraints already shape the work. We will help identify the useful path.</p><div class="callout__actions"><a class="text-link" href="/playable-ads/release-quality-platform-readiness/">See the readiness package <span>↗</span></a><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss a playable</button></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
